<!-- AREAS -->
<section style="padding:76px 24px 60px;background:#fff;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
    <span class="kicker">Service Areas</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,36px);margin:0 0 16px;">Serving Nigeria</h2>
    <div class="rich" style="text-align:left;"><p>We mobilise from Lagos to industrial sites across six states, and our hub pages set out the duty conditions, common failure modes and access constraints we meet in each. Work is covered in <a href="/turbine-services-lagos/">Lagos</a> across the Ikeja, Agbara, Ikorodu and Apapa belts, in <a href="/turbine-services-port-harcourt/">Port Harcourt</a> and the Rivers State oil and gas corridor, in <a href="/turbine-services-abuja/">Abuja</a> and the FCT, in <a href="/turbine-services-kaduna/">Kaduna</a>, in <a href="/turbine-services-warri/">Warri</a> and Delta State, and in <a href="/turbine-services-kano/">Kano</a> where harmattan dust loading drives much of the derating we are asked to correct. Sites outside these states are considered case by case, based on machine class, duration and access.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#EAF5FB;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Which turbines and generators do you work on?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Back pressure and condensing steam turbines running alongside boiler plant, industrial and aeroderivative gas turbines, and diesel and gas generator sets from a few hundred kVA up to synchronised multi megawatt banks. We also cover the driven and auxiliary equipment on the same train, including pumps, centrifugal and screw compressors, ID and FD fans, blowers and gearboxes. If you send the make, model, rating and running hours with your enquiry, we will confirm before a site visit whether the machine sits inside our scope.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How does pricing and scoping work?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Nothing is priced before the machine is assessed, because scope is what drives cost on rotating equipment. A site survey or plant assessment establishes condition, and the resulting proposal separates mobilisation, manpower and duration, spares and consumables with lead times, and any specialist services such as balancing or machining, each priced in Naira so lines can be compared against other bids. As an indication, a single machine plant assessment typically falls in the 1.2 million to 3.5 million Naira band (roughly 800 to 2,300 US dollars) depending on machine class, location and how much historical data exists, while overhaul cost is governed by inspection level and parts condition. Our turbine and generator maintenance cost guide explains how those elements build up.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">What are your response and lead times?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Enquiries are answered the same working day and an engineer will normally speak with your maintenance team within 24 hours to establish urgency. Site surveys in Lagos are typically arranged within a week, and within one to two weeks for Rivers, FCT, Kaduna, Delta and Kano depending on access and permit requirements. The written proposal follows within five to seven working days of the survey. Execution dates depend mainly on spares: consumables and common bearings move quickly, while nozzles, diaphragms, blading and control components can carry lead times of several weeks, which is why long lead items are flagged in the proposal rather than discovered mid outage.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Can the work be completed inside our planned outage window?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">That is decided at the survey stage, not on the day of mobilisation. We build the scope backwards from your window, identify the critical path and the hold points, and confirm whether the full work list fits or whether it should be split across two outages. Where the window is genuinely too short, we will say so in writing and propose the safe subset plus the items that can be deferred with a defined inspection interval.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Do you supply spares, or do we procure them ourselves?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Either arrangement works and both are priced transparently. Where we supply, the proposal lists each item, its specification and its expected lead time, so you can see which parts decide the schedule. Where your procurement team prefers to buy directly, we issue the specifications and drawings needed to order correctly and review what arrives before it goes near the machine.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">What documentation do we receive at the end of a job?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">A handover file containing as found and as left readings, vibration and alignment data, borescope observations where taken, clearance and torque records, the list of parts replaced and parts returned, and any deviations agreed during the work. It closes with recommended inspection intervals and a watch list of items to monitor before the next window. That file is written to support your maintenance plan, budget submissions and technical queries from insurers or lenders.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

